M04_Objective_Controller_JDG soft-lock: missile briefing dropped by a key
conversation. Announce 440 sets missile_primary_active and starts the
non-key M04_Add_MissileRoom_Objective_Conversation. Only its ENDED callback
adds objective 300 and sends M01_START_ACTING_JDG to the four racks; the racks
ignore pokes until then. ActiveConversationClass::Start_Conversation stops a
non-key conversation at once (INTERRUPTED) while a key conversation plays, and
that happens before Monitor_Conversation registers the controller, so no
callback ever arrives. M04 key conversations (m04.ldd VARID_ISKEY) include
M04_Add_Captains_Key_Objective_Conversation and
M04_Prisoner_Guard_is_in_Medlab_Conversation. Entering the missile-room zone
while one of them plays left the racks unpokable and the mission incompletable.
Schedule a self-custom (441) 20 s after the announcement; the briefing lasts
about 8.2 s (two remarks). If the end callback has not run by then, run the
original end-of-briefing step. A new flag (unused save id 48) makes the step
run once. When the briefing ends normally the original branch runs unchanged
and the fallback does nothing.

